{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CghAX42SVNt25KXLkojp5", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**NotificationsService stores its data in NotificationsRedisInstance.** The graph has one direct edge for this: `NotificationsService -STORES-> NotificationsRedisInstance`.\n\n**What it stores isn't recorded.** The graph links the service to the Redis instance but doesn't say what kind of data it keeps there (for example queued notifications, delivery state or a cache). It also has no further storage or dependency edges, even at depth 3. So NotificationsRedisInstance is the only data store I can confirm. The service's code or schema would show what's actually in it.\n\n**Configuration:** One key configures NotificationsService: `RETRY_ATTEMPTS`. It sets \"three attempts with a 250ms backoff\". The graph doesn't tie it to storage, so it may cover outbound calls or delivery rather than Redis writes.\n\n**Names involved:**\n- Service: NotificationsService\n- Database: NotificationsRedisInstance (Redis)\n- Config key: RETRY_ATTEMPTS\n- APIs: none appear in its dependencies"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 188, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4800, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 188}, "output_tokens": 350, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5cacfdc4-f6fb-4c28-ab72-9d295d312dfd", "uuid": "ba2df7dd-da3f-4bf7-a3eb-fa3603b16d0c", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T03:18:33.304Z", "request_id": "req_011CghAX3oJvmMHRQV6dHLKs"}
